  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "simple-adj",
      "easy-adj"
    ],
    "note": "**Easy** is about effort: something easy needs little work or skill (*an easy exam*, *an easy win*). **Simple** is about how something is made or said: it has few parts or steps, so it is easy to understand (*a simple question*, *simple instructions*). Often both words fit. Use **simple**, not **easy**, for plain things such as clothes or food: *a simple dress*."
  },
